<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hog - Tuesday estimate 110,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hog - Tuesday estimate 110,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Barrows and gilts steady compared with mid-session Monday. Trade moderate for moderate demand and offerings.</p>
<p>Tuesday's  estimate:  110000  Wk ago:  110000  Yr ago: 110000</p>
<p>Estimates include generally about 60 percent Carcass Base Hogs.</p>
<p>US 1-3 46-49% Carcass Base Lean*  Country	   Plants</p>
<p>	  220-260 lbs		53.50 -55.00    54.50 -56.00</p>
<p>	  few			  52.50 -53.00    53.50 -54.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>	  260-280 lbs		51.50 -55.00    52.00 -56.00</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>	  280-300 lbs		48.00 -53.50    48.50 -54.50</p>
<p>Sows:  mostly steady to 2.00 higher.</p>
<p>US 1-3  300-450 lbs.	     43.50 -46.00    44.50 -46.00</p>
<p>	  450-500 lbs.	     48.00 -52.00    49.00 -53.00</p>
<p>	  500 lbs. up		54.00 -60.00    55.00 -61.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct. carcass. Yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct. lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720--</p>
</text>
